    <string name="privacy_intro">Your privacy matters. This policy explains what the app accesses and why. In short: everything stays on your device.</string>
    <string-array name="privacy_titles">
        <item>Data we access</item>
        <item>How your data is used</item>
        <item>No internet, no ads</item>
        <item>Blocked numbers</item>
        <item>Your choices</item>
        <item>Changes</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="privacy_bodies">
        <item>With your permission, the app reads and edits your contacts and call history, places calls, and shows notifications. Photos you pick for a contact are only used to set that contact\'s picture.</item>
        <item>Your data is used only to show your contacts, calls and caller names inside the app. It is processed on your device and is never uploaded, sold or shared.</item>
        <item>The app does not request internet access, contains no ads and uses no analytics or tracking tools.</item>
        <item>Blocked numbers are stored in Android\'s system block list so they keep working with your phone\'s other features.</item>
        <item>You can revoke any permission at any time in your phone\'s settings. Settings you choose in the app are stored only on this device and are removed when you uninstall it.</item>
        <item>If this policy changes, the updated version will be included in an app update.</item>
    </string-array>

